Root cause: PR check workflow `🔍 Lint & Test` (.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml) has run on every PR since 2025-07-03, but was not enforced as a *required* status check until the `Main branch rules` ruleset (id 13779853) was created on normainofficial/normain on 2026-03-11. The 78 flagged PRs were merged before that date, when no enforced requirement existed (the check ran and passed, but was not blocking).

Remediation in place (2026-03-11 → 2026-04-28):
1. Active ruleset on `main` requires `🔍 Lint & Test` + 1 PR review + linear history + squash merges. Source: https://github.com/normainofficial/normain/rules/13779853
2. Bypass actors hardened on 2026-04-28: removed direct user bypasses (PhilipNgo, redsuperbat); admin role downgraded to `pull_request` mode (no direct push); only `normain-ci-bot` retains `always` bypass for the automated `tenants.json` commit in `provision-tenants.yml` (scoped GitHub App, contents:write only).
3. CODEOWNERS added (PR #1977); ruleset will require code-owner review + conversation resolution after merge.
4. All other org repos (21x) archived 2026-04-28 — only `normain` is in scope.

Compensating evidence: 600/600 sampled PRs (pre- and post-ruleset) had `🔍 Lint & Test` pass before merge — the control was effectively in place culturally; this remediation makes it formally enforced.

Deactivating these 78 historical PRs indefinitely: they are already merged and cannot retroactively be re-checked; future PRs are covered by the ruleset above.
